     fhir:CodeSystem.concept.definition [ fhir:value "Atrial baffle procedure for rerouting of venous flow in TGA effecting a \"physiological repair\".  The caval flow is directed behind the baffle to the mitral valve, left ventricle and pulmonary artery while pulmonary venous flow is directed in front of the baffle to the tricuspid valve, right ventricle, and aorta. The Mustard procedure uses patch material to construct the baffle." ] ;
